   "daf": "20a",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "וּכְשֶׁמַּבְרִין אוֹתוֹ כּוּ׳. מַאי דַּרְגֵּשׁ? אָמַר עוּלָּא: עַרְסָא דְּגַדָּא. אֲמַרוּ לֵיהּ רַבָּנַן לְעוּלָּא: מִי אִיכָּא מִידֵּי דְּעַד הָאִידָּנָא לָא אוֹתְבִינֵּיהּ, וְהַשְׁתָּא מוֹתְבִינַן לֵיהּ?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And when they comfort» the king with the meal of comfort, he reclines on the dargash. The Gemara asks: «What» is «a dargash? Ulla says: A bed of fortune,» which would be designated in houses for decoration and for good fortune, and no one would sit on it. «The Sages said to Ulla: Is there anything» which «until now we did not authorize one to sit» on, «but now,» in his time of mourning, «we seat him» on it?"
  }
